      "score": 0.528456,
      "passage": "Options considered: keep per-display autonomy with a better flashing ritual;\none edge gateway per station coordinating its displays."
    },
    {
      "path": "decisions/d-109.md",
      "para": 1,
      "score": 0.523295,
      "passage": "Options considered: keep per-display autonomy with a better flashing ritual;\none edge relay per station coordinating its displays."
    },
    {
      "path": "decisions/d-002.md",
      "para": 0,
      "score": 0.521387,
      "passage": "Context: platform displays need live vehicle positions with sub-second\nperceived freshness; HTTP polling burns battery and lags."
    },
    {
      "path": "decisions/d-002.md",
      "para": 2,
      "score": 0.521271,
      "passage": "Decision: the Wayfare display fleet speaks MQTT 3.1.1 to a transit-side\nbroker; retained messages let a display recover its last-known state after\nreconnect. Informed by mqtt-311-notes."
    },
    {
      "path": "projects/perchboard.md",
      "para": 1,
      "score": 0.520418,
      "passage": "Scope agreed at the kickoff (2025-09-29) with Dara Whitlock: sub-second\nperceived freshness, outdoor readability, and a May ship date. The displays\nspeak MQTT 5.0 (decision d-102) and went from per-display autonomy (d-103)\nto an edge relay per station (d-109) after field maintenance pain. The\npalette is high-contrast white-on-black (d-112), with fleet clocks kept\nhonest by chrony (d-110)."
    },
    {
      "path": "sessions/s-004.md",
      "para": 0,
      "score": 0.510263,
      "passage": "Theo and Dev spent the day in the field at Ashport Central and Ferry Quay:\nafter the last firmware update, the three pilot stations drifted to three\nfirmware versions, and a board that lost power would not recover its clock.\nReflashing takes roughly ninety minutes per display carried to the platform.\nPer-display autonomy (d-003) is failing on maintenance, not on rendering."
    },
    {
      "path": "projects/wayfare.md",
      "para": 1,
      "score": 0.508388,
      "passage": "Scope agreed at the kickoff (2026-02-20) with Petra Lindqvist: sub-second\nperceived freshness, outdoor readability, and a June ship date. The displays\nspeak MQTT (decision d-002) and went from per-display autonomy (d-003) to an\nedge-gateway hub (d-008) after field maintenance pain. The palette is\ngreen-and-amber for outdoor readability (d-009)."
    },
    {
      "path": "meetings/m-005.md",
      "para": 0,
      "score": 0.507425,
      "passage": "Architecture review on the field findings (s-004): three firmware versions\nacross three stations, ninety-minute reflashes per display. Theo proposed the\nedge-gateway hub — flash once per station, displays pull from the gateway —\nover keeping per-display autonomy with a better flashing ritual. The room\nagreed, and d-008 landed the same day. Bram takes gateway provisioning."
    },
    {
      "path": "decisions/d-002.md",
      "para": 3,
      "score": 0.502399,
      "passage": "Consequences: one broker to operate at Halcyon; occasional QoS-1 duplicate\nrenders, accepted for freshness."
    },
    {
      "path": "references/fleet-provisioning-notes.md",
      "para": 0,
      "score": 0.502387,
      "passage": "Provisioning a fleet of small boards two ways: point-wise flashing scales\nlinearly with board count and fails quietly; a gateway-hub topology flashes\nonce per site and funnels telemetry home. The hub costs one more box per\nstation but collapses the maintenance surface."
    }
  ]
}

